{"findings":[{"criterionId":"cohesion","observation":"Your essay is organised around the three reasons, and signposts like \"First of all\", \"Another reason is\" and \"Last reason why\" help the reader follow the structure. Some connections are unclear, though. The sentence \"Because, they are not financially good with money\" does not clearly link to the point before it, and the last body paragraph repeats ideas instead of developing them. Clearer linking words and a more precise explanation of how each reason connects to the main claim would strengthen the flow.","excerpts":[{"artifact":"work","quote":"First of all one reason that it may be good"},{"artifact":"work","quote":"Because, they are not financially good with money."},{"artifact":"work","quote":"Last reason why students may want to graduate early"}],"uncertainty":"medium"},{"criterionId":"syntax","observation":"Most of your sentences are simple or compound, which makes your ideas easy to follow. Try combining short sentences and controlling longer ones more carefully. The sentence beginning \"If students need to help there families out\" joins several clauses with \"and\" and no punctuation, so it becomes hard to read. Using a mix of sentence lengths and some subordinate clauses would show more control.","excerpts":[{"artifact":"work","quote":"If students need to help there families out and they finish with school early they dont have to worry about having to go to school they can just work so that they can help there families out."},{"artifact":"work","quote":"So if they finish school in three years they can start working at a full-time job early"}],"uncertainty":"medium"},{"criterionId":"vocabulary","observation":"You communicate your ideas clearly, but your word choice is often general and repetitive. \"Early\" and \"get over with\" appear many times, and phrases like \"keep on going to school\" could be more precise. Using more specific words, such as \"accelerate\", \"well-paid\" or \"obligation\", would make your arguments more persuasive and varied.","excerpts":[{"artifact":"work","quote":"Students would love to finish school in three years because they dont want to keep on going to school."},{"artifact":"work","quote":"Students may know what they want to become when they are older"}],"uncertainty":"medium"},{"criterionId":"phraseology","observation":"You use some useful expressions, such as \"help out\" and \"start making money\", and these work well in context. Other combinations sound unnatural, such as \"a good financial job\", which is more naturally expressed as \"a well-paid job\" or \"a stable career\". Also, \"get that over with\" is informal for an argumentative essay. Learning standard collocations for academic writing would make your language sound more natural.","excerpts":[{"artifact":"work","quote":"get that over with at a early age and get a good financial job"},{"artifact":"work","quote":"Students sometimes just want to start making money"}],"uncertainty":"medium"},{"criterionId":"grammar","observation":"Your sentences are mostly understandable, but there are recurring errors. \"There\" is used where \"their\" is needed, several nouns and verbs do not agree, and the article \"a\" is used before a vowel sound. Check the agreement in \"Some school district offer programs\" and \"these are three good reason\", and use \"their\" for possession, \"by themselves\" for reflexive pronouns, and \"them\" as the object pronoun. Reviewing these points will improve your accuracy considerably.","excerpts":[{"artifact":"work","quote":"Some school district offer programs"},{"artifact":"work","quote":"they may need to help there family out"},{"artifact":"work","quote":"these are three good reason why students would like to finish high school in three years"},{"artifact":"work","quote":"it would benefit they if they could finish high school in three years"}],"uncertainty":"low"},{"criterionId":"conventions","observation":"Your ideas are readable, but spelling and punctuation need attention. Contractions are missing their apostrophes (\"dont\"), possessives are misused (\"family's\" and \"students parents\"), and some commas are placed incorrectly (\"Because, they are\"). Also, the spelling \"there\" for \"their\" appears often. Proofreading for these specific points would make your writing look more polished.","excerpts":[{"artifact":"work","quote":"they dont have to worry about having to go to school"},{"artifact":"work","quote":"help out there family's"},{"artifact":"work","quote":"The students parents may work"},{"artifact":"work","quote":"Because, they are not financially good with money."}],"uncertainty":"low"}]}
