{"findings":[{"criterionId":"cohesion","observation":"You use a good range of linking words and phrases, such as \"Firstable,\", \"Also,\", \"On the other hand,\" and \"Consequently,\", which help the reader follow your structure. Some connections are unclear, though. In your second body paragraph, \"For examples\" introduces a point that doesn't clearly follow from the idea before it, and in the first paragraph the link between the girl's story and your claim is left implicit. Also, the referent of \"that\" is often unclear, so consider naming the idea directly to make each link explicit.","excerpts":[{"artifact":"work","quote":"Firstable, I think the students to attend classes from home"},{"artifact":"work","quote":"On the other hand, the online class is not really useless thing that for the students."},{"artifact":"work","quote":"Consequently, every students who enjoy that much, they could take that class much easily to study in their home."}],"uncertainty":"medium"},{"criterionId":"syntax","observation":"You attempt a variety of structures, including subordinate clauses and sentences that begin with linking adverbials. Several sentences, however, are long and tangled, with multiple clauses joined by commas where the grammatical relationship between them is hard to follow. Breaking some of these into shorter, clearer sentences, or using subordination more deliberately, would give you better control of your sentence structure.","excerpts":[{"artifact":"work","quote":"Because, there are many reasons that the students could not able to learn home by yourself in online"},{"artifact":"work","quote":"Also, it will be impact their behaviour that they'll be more lonely."},{"artifact":"work","quote":"Because the students behaivior is always changing and easy to get used to their environment"}],"uncertainty":"low"},{"criterionId":"vocabulary","observation":"You have a reasonable base of topic vocabulary, such as \"online,\" \"video conferencing,\" \"communicate\" and \"environment.\" To improve precision, look for more exact words. For example, \"advantegious\" is a word you are trying to reach for, and \"understable\" would be better expressed as \"understandable\" or, more precisely, \"easier to understand.\" Choosing more specific verbs and adjectives in place of general ones such as \"more\" would also strengthen your expression.","excerpts":[{"artifact":"work","quote":"Of course, It should be has some advantegious way to attend online and video class"},{"artifact":"work","quote":"they cannot learn that more understable."}],"uncertainty":"low"},{"criterionId":"phraseology","observation":"You use some useful expressions, such as \"hold one point of view\" and \"give up to study alone.\" Some collocations need adjusting, however. \"Catch up\" is usually followed by \"on\" or \"with\" (for example, \"catch up on late work\"), and \"give up\" is normally followed by a verb in the -ing form (\"give up studying alone\"). Practising these fixed phrases will make your writing sound more natural.","excerpts":[{"artifact":"work","quote":"they migth cannot catch up their late works"},{"artifact":"work","quote":"we don't have to hold one point of view"},{"artifact":"work","quote":"students might be trying to give up to study alone"}],"uncertainty":"medium"},{"criterionId":"grammar","observation":"Your writing communicates your ideas, but there are recurring problems with agreement, verb forms and word forms. Examples include the verb form after \"could\" and \"can't\", the subject-verb agreement in \"she have\", and the use of \"every\" with a plural noun. Also, the word \"impact\" is used as a verb without the correct form. Reviewing these patterns will help your sentences become more accurate.","excerpts":[{"artifact":"work","quote":"the students could not able to learn home by yourself in online"},{"artifact":"work","quote":"she didn't study as well as can't catch up her study work"},{"artifact":"work","quote":"she have to her exam in the school"},{"artifact":"work","quote":"the every students are different way to study"}],"uncertainty":"low"},{"criterionId":"conventions","observation":"Your essay has several spelling errors and inconsistent punctuation and capitalisation. Words such as \"Firstable,\" \"thier,\" \"behaivior\" and \"studehts\" need correcting. The pronoun \"I\" should be capitalised in all positions, and sentences should not start with a capital letter after a comma. Careful proofreading, especially of commonly misspelt words, will make a clear difference to how your writing is received.","excerpts":[{"artifact":"work","quote":"Firstable, I think the students to attend classes from home"},{"artifact":"work","quote":"Because the students behaivior is always changing"},{"artifact":"work","quote":"Therefore, i disagree to attend classes from home"},{"artifact":"work","quote":"the student might think very well to thier option"}],"uncertainty":"low"}]}
