{"findings":[{"criterionId":"cohesion","observation":"Your transition words (First, Next, Also, In conclusion) make the structure of the essay easy to follow. The link between the vegetables example and your main point is weaker, though. Explain how the example supports the claim about healthy lunches, and consider using a reference word or linking phrase to connect the ideas more clearly.","excerpts":[{"artifact":"work","quote":"First, having a healthier school lunch in the school cafeteria will give students a healthy long life."},{"artifact":"work","quote":"For example, if a student eats vegetable he/she will have much more clear blood than a student who eats meat."}],"uncertainty":"medium"},{"criterionId":"syntax","observation":"Most of your sentences follow a similar simple pattern. Some longer sentences join several ideas with commas and 'and' without clear boundaries, which makes them harder to read. Try combining short sentences with subordinate clauses (because, although, when) and using semicolons or separate sentences where a comma splice appears.","excerpts":[{"artifact":"work","quote":"Students will be able to perform better, they will live a longer and healthier life and students will be in a good shape"},{"artifact":"work","quote":"They won't have any blood pressure problems."}],"uncertainty":"medium"},{"criterionId":"vocabulary","observation":"You use clear everyday words such as 'healthy', 'tired' and 'impact'. To make your writing more precise, choose words that say exactly what you mean. For example, 'clear blood' is unclear; you could say 'cleaner blood' or 'better blood circulation' instead. Varying words like 'good' and 'better' would also add range.","excerpts":[{"artifact":"work","quote":"foods that are healthier will have a huge impact on students performance"},{"artifact":"work","quote":"will have much more clear blood than a student who eats meat"}],"uncertainty":"medium"},{"criterionId":"phraseology","observation":"You use some useful expressions, such as 'in good shape' and 'live a longer life'. Some collocations need correction: 'pay a lots of money' should be 'pay a lot of money', and 'going to doctor' should be 'going to the doctor' or 'visiting a doctor'. Learning common fixed phrases will help your writing sound more natural.","excerpts":[{"artifact":"work","quote":"pay a lots of money"},{"artifact":"work","quote":"keeps you away from going to doctor as often"}],"uncertainty":"medium"},{"criterionId":"grammar","observation":"Several errors affect agreement and word forms. 'Students' needs' should be 'students need' to match the plural subject. 'A lots' should be 'a lot'. 'Vegetable' should be 'vegetables' after 'a student eats'. Also check 'there' and 'their': 'There body' and 'there brain' should use 'their'.","excerpts":[{"artifact":"work","quote":"most of the students needs to eat healthy"},{"artifact":"work","quote":"There body will be able to preform better as there brain."},{"artifact":"work","quote":"if a student eats vegetable he/she"}],"uncertainty":"high"},{"criterionId":"conventions","observation":"Your ideas are easy to follow, but there are several spelling and punctuation errors to check. 'Preform' should be 'perform', and 'there' should be 'their' when showing possession. 'Students performance' needs an apostrophe ('students' performance'). Capitalise only the first word of a sentence, so 'Students' in the middle of a sentence should be lowercase.","excerpts":[{"artifact":"work","quote":"students will preform better in the school activities"},{"artifact":"work","quote":"will have a huge impact on students performance"},{"artifact":"work","quote":"Also, Students will not be sick as often"},{"artifact":"work","quote":"pay a lots of money for there body which they can control"}],"uncertainty":"low"}]}
