{"findings":[{"criterionId":"cohesion","observation":"Your body paragraphs each open by restating a point from the introduction, which gives the essay a clear structure. However, the paragraphs are connected mainly by repetition rather than by transitions that show how each idea relates to the argument. Adding linking phrases (for example, 'Furthermore' or 'In contrast') and tying the final paragraph back to your opening claim would strengthen the flow. Pronoun use also shifts between 'the person', 'it', and 'they', so keeping one consistent reference would help the reader follow.","suggestedLevel":"l3","excerpts":[{"artifact":"work","quote":"Being different can isolate someone from the society and this can change a persons life choice."},{"artifact":"work","quote":"The person can act freely and become who it wants to be also they do not have to worry about peer pressure."}],"uncertainty":"medium"},{"criterionId":"syntax","observation":"You use a variety of sentence openings, such as 'Being able to...' and 'Not letting people...', which is a good start. Several sentences, though, join separate ideas without punctuation or connectors, which makes them hard to follow. Breaking these into shorter sentences or linking them with clear conjunctions would give you more control over your sentence structures.","suggestedLevel":"l2","excerpts":[{"artifact":"work","quote":"The person can act freely and become who it wants to be also they do not have to worry about peer pressure."},{"artifact":"work","quote":"not letting people influence a person characteristics is a big accomplishment, having to be someone who a person wants to become can show the person full capability"}],"uncertainty":"medium"},{"criterionId":"vocabulary","observation":"You use some effective academic words, such as 'originality', 'isolate', and 'capability', which add precision to your ideas. You also rely on the same phrase several times, such as 'a big', which narrows your range. Choosing more specific alternatives (for example, 'significant impact' or 'considerable advantage') would show a wider vocabulary.","suggestedLevel":"l3","excerpts":[{"artifact":"work","quote":"Being different can isolate someone from the society"},{"artifact":"work","quote":"can give a big advantage in creativity"},{"artifact":"work","quote":"can make a big impact on a persons life"}],"uncertainty":"medium"},{"criterionId":"phraseology","observation":"Some of your word combinations sound natural, such as 'peer pressure' and 'worry about what others think'. Other combinations are less conventional in English. 'Full capability' is usually expressed as 'full potential', and 'is complete fine' would be more natural as 'is completely fine'. Reading widely in academic writing will help you learn which combinations are typical.","suggestedLevel":"l2","excerpts":[{"artifact":"work","quote":"can show the person full capability"},{"artifact":"work","quote":"To be someone that a persons dont want to become is complete fine"}],"uncertainty":"medium"},{"criterionId":"grammar","observation":"There are several agreement and verb-form errors to focus on. Subjects and verbs do not always agree, for example 'rules that needs' and 'The person do not have'. Some verbs are missing the correct form, such as 'to be follow' and 'suppose' (which should be 'supposed'). Also, 'the persons have' should be 'the person has' or 'the persons have' depending on the intended subject. Reviewing subject-verb agreement and verb forms after 'to be' and modal verbs will help.","suggestedLevel":"l2","excerpts":[{"artifact":"work","quote":"The world has many rules that needs to be follow"},{"artifact":"work","quote":"The person do not have to worry about what others think of whats it can do."},{"artifact":"work","quote":"Being able to be someone who the person is not suppose to be"}],"uncertainty":"medium"},{"criterionId":"conventions","observation":"Your ideas are clear, but spelling and punctuation errors often interrupt the reading. Words such as 'whethere', 'accomplisment', 'becase', and 'no body' need correcting. Possessive apostrophes are missing in phrases such as 'a persons life', and some sentences need capital letters or commas, such as 'because Being able'. Proofreading for these specific patterns, particularly possessives and spelling, would make a noticeable difference.","suggestedLevel":"l2","excerpts":[{"artifact":"work","quote":"whethere it's a good thing or bad"},{"artifact":"work","quote":"the biggest accomplisment in a persons life becase acting different"},{"artifact":"work","quote":"because Being able to be someone who the person is not suppose to be"}],"uncertainty":"low"}]}
