{"findings":[{"criterionId":"cohesion","observation":"Your essay has a clear structure: an introduction, three body paragraphs that each develop one idea, and a conclusion that sums up your argument. Transitions such as \"For example\", \"Another reason why\" and \"In conclusion\" guide the reader well. To strengthen cohesion, check the connecting phrases. \"in the other hand\" should be \"on the other hand\", and \"In overall\" should be \"Overall\". Adding a space after the comma in \"do,in the other hand\" would also help the reader follow the contrast.","excerpts":[{"artifact":"work","quote":"For example if you encounter the same situation as them you'll know what to do,in the other hand if you didn't pay attention to them"},{"artifact":"work","quote":"In overall if someone is trying to talk to you about their past experiences"},{"artifact":"work","quote":"Another reason why it could be important to listen to someone's past experiences is so you don't make the same mistakes as them."}],"uncertainty":"medium"},{"criterionId":"syntax","observation":"You use a good mix of simple and compound sentences, and some longer sentences join ideas with \"if\", \"because\" and \"so\". To extend your range, try breaking up long chains of clauses joined by \"and\" or \"then\". For example, the grandpa sentence could be split into two or three sentences. Using more varied complex structures, such as sentences beginning with subordinate clauses, would also add variety.","excerpts":[{"artifact":"work","quote":"When I was 8 years old my grandpa used to tell me that smoking wasn't good at all even tho he did it all the time,then my dad told me the same thing about smoking"},{"artifact":"work","quote":"In conclusion I think that listening to other people's past experiences is good because it will help a lot in the future and it'll help you make important decisions in life"}],"uncertainty":"medium"},{"criterionId":"vocabulary","observation":"You choose clear, mostly appropriate words such as \"encounter\", \"clueless\" and \"struggling\", which show precision. Some words are vague or incorrect in this context. \"stuff\" is general, \"past\" should replace \"back\" in \"other people back experiences\", and \"pick in between\" could be more precise. Try to choose words that express your exact meaning, such as \"choose between\" for the decision idea.","excerpts":[{"artifact":"work","quote":"to make a decision or to pick in between stuff"},{"artifact":"work","quote":"I think it's really interesting to hear about other people back experiences"},{"artifact":"work","quote":"If a friend is in trouble or he needs advice with something you could help them out"}],"uncertainty":"medium"},{"criterionId":"phraseology","observation":"You use several useful collocations correctly, such as \"pay close attention\", \"make a decision\", \"help them out\" and \"make the same mistake\". Some fixed expressions need correcting: \"come handy\" should be \"come in handy\", \"in overall\" should be \"overall\", \"in the other hand\" should be \"on the other hand\", and \"pick in between\" is not a standard expression. Learning these set phrases as complete chunks will make your writing sound more natural.","excerpts":[{"artifact":"work","quote":"you should pay close attention because it could come handy in life"},{"artifact":"work","quote":"In overall if someone is trying to talk to you"},{"artifact":"work","quote":"in the other hand if you didn't pay attention to them"},{"artifact":"work","quote":"I won't make the same mistake my grandpa did"}],"uncertainty":"medium"},{"criterionId":"grammar","observation":"Most of your grammar is accurate, including tense use in the grandpa story and the conditional structures. The main error is confusing \"it's\" (it is) with \"its\" (possessive). Also check word forms: \"come handy\" needs \"come in handy\". Keep checking your verb and pronoun forms as you write, especially in longer sentences.","excerpts":[{"artifact":"work","quote":"I'll always know that smoking it's not good for anyone's health"},{"artifact":"work","quote":"it could come handy in life"}],"uncertainty":"medium"},{"criterionId":"conventions","observation":"Your ideas are easy to follow, but punctuation needs attention. Add commas after introductory words such as \"Well\", and place commas before clauses such as \"then my dad\" and \"in the other hand\", with a space after them. Avoid informal spellings such as \"tho\" and \"Well\" at the start of a formal essay. Also use \"it's\" only for \"it is\" and \"its\" for possession. Check your spacing and comma use during editing.","excerpts":[{"artifact":"work","quote":"Well it could help you in the future to make a decision or to pick in between stuff."},{"artifact":"work","quote":"even tho he did it all the time,then my dad told me the same thing"},{"artifact":"work","quote":"you'll know what to do,in the other hand"}],"uncertainty":"medium"}]}
